{title: Migdalor Ba’arafel}
{artist: Galei Nachal Band}
{key: Am}
{meta: language he-Latn}

{comment: Intro}
[Am]/ / / | [D]/ / / | [G]/ / / | [Em]/ / /

{comment: Verse 1}
[Am]Migdalor omed [D]al ha’sela
(A lighthouse stands on the rock)
[G]Or katan [Em]be’tokh ha’arafel
(A small light inside the fog)
[Am]Sira mi’Tel Aviv [D]mekhapeset khof
(A boat from Tel Aviv looks for shore)
[G]Ve’ha’lev [Em]lo pokhed
(And the heart is not afraid)

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Laila shaket [G]al ha’yam
(A quiet night upon the sea)
[Am]Kol ha’laila [F]ani shomer
(All night long I keep watch)
[C]Or ekhad [G]lo kava
(One light has not gone out)
[Am]Ad she’yavo [E7]ha’boker
(Until the morning comes)

{comment: Verse 2}
[Am]Galim ba’im [D]ve’galim holkhim
(Waves come and waves go)
[G]Ha’khevel [Em]makhzik khazak
(The rope holds strong)
[Am]Mi she’ma'amin [D]ba’ner katan
(Whoever believes in a small candle)
[G]Yagi'a [Em]ha’bayta laʼad
(Will arrive home forever)
